Cell["\<\
On a canonical Lie bialgebra with the empty word, the empty word is among the \
words tested.\
\>", "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"c9adeffa-9cb1-4056-9e8c-03515afaaa7e"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "With ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 ", the test is finite: it says the relations hold in that range, not that \
they hold. For an A-infinity algebra whose operations vanish above some \
arity, a large enough ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 " is conclusive."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"830e2465-ee32-486d-a5c2-754173d6d290"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "On a complex, a decomposition and a propagator the structure is finite and \
the relations multilinear, so the test is complete and takes no ",
 StyleBox["n", "TI"],
 "."
}], "Notes",ExpressionUUID->"27ffad7a-9404-4f5e-bc89-f0167db41152"],

